{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TpeGTtjyNFfTfuZZB4MPjR","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Scenario Builder — Summary\n2\t\n3\t## Bug Fix\n4\t\n5\t### Priority 1 — IDA* heuristic reads wrong radio group\n6\t- **File:** `visual/js/panel.js:160`\n7\t- **Fix:** Changed `$('input[name=jump_point_heuristic]:checked')` → `$('input[name=ida_heuristic]:checked')`\n8\t- **Impact:** IDA* panel was reading JPS heuristic radio group instead of its own. User-selected heuristic in IDA* section was ignored.\n9\t\n10\t## Test Scenarios Created\n11\t\n12\t**File:** `test/VisualScenarios.js` — 39 tests across 14 priority scenarios.\n13\t\n14\t| Priority | Scenario | Tests | Status |\n15\t|----------|----------|-------|--------|\n16\t| 1 | IDA* heuristic independence | 2 | ✅ Pass |\n17\t| 2 | No path found (start surrounded) | 4 | ✅ Pass |\n18\t| 3 | Start equals end | 5 | ✅ Pass |\n19\t| 4 | Drag during search (state machine) | 1 | ✅ Documented |\n20\t| 5 | Wall on start/end position | 4 | ✅ Pass |\n21\t| 6 | Pause/Resume cycle | 1 | ✅ Documented |\n22\t| 7 | Restart during search | 1 | ✅ Documented |\n23\t| 8 | JPS all 4 diagonal modes | 4 | ✅ Pass |\n24\t| 9 | Bi-directional vs unidirectional | 1 | ✅ Pass |\n25\t| 10 | Weight parameter effect | 1 | ✅ Pass |\n26\t| 11 | IDA* time limit | 3 | ✅ Pass |\n27\t| 12 | Full grid walls | 3 | ✅ Pass |\n28\t| 13 | Large grid performance (64×36) | 2 | ✅ Pass |\n29\t| 14 | Adjacent start/end | 4 | ✅ Pass |\n30\t\n31\t## Key Findings\n32\t\n33\t1. **Finders don't validate start/end walkability.** They push start into open list unconditionally. Visual app handles this via `isStartOrEndPos` guard in `mousedown` handler.\n34\t\n35\t2. **JPS UI gap confirmed.** Only `IfAtMostOneObstacle` and `Never` exposed. `Always` and `OnlyWhenNoObstacles` work at library level but need UI dropdown to be selectable. Panel.js hardcodes `DiagonalMovement.IfAtMostOneObstacle` at line 139.\n36\t\n37\t3. **State machine correctly guards drag.** `dragStart`/`dragEnd` only allowed from `ready`/`finished` states. No drag possible during `searching`/`paused`.\n38\t\n39\t4. **Pause/resume is clean.** `loop()` checks `Controller.is('searching')` — pausing stops the loop, resume re-enters it from same operations array position.\n40\t\n41\t5. **No \"path not found\" UI feedback.** `view.js:drawPath` returns silently on empty path. `showStats` shows `length: 0` but no explicit message. This is a UI gap, not a library bug.\n42\t\n43\t## Full Suite Result\n44\t\n45\t```\n46\t256 passing (1s)\n47\t0 failing\n48\t```\n49\t\n50\tNo regressions introduced.\n51\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fb2c7ec1-8b93-4f0c-93e3-1380bfdce95e","uuid":"dfd03145-0613-4507-9097-9003184ff9d5","timestamp":"2026-04-16T14:11:27.843Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/sagar/template-repo/docs/experiments/001-demo-artifacts/fleets/fleet-01-test-blitz/workers/scenario-builder/output/summary.md","content":"# Scenario Builder — Summary\n\n## Bug Fix\n\n### Priority 1 — IDA* heuristic reads wrong radio group\n- **File:** `visual/js/panel.js:160`\n- **Fix:** Changed `$('input[name=jump_point_heuristic]:checked')` → `$('input[name=ida_heuristic]:checked')`\n- **Impact:** IDA* panel was reading JPS heuristic radio group instead of its own. User-selected heuristic in IDA* section was ignored.\n\n## Test Scenarios Created\n\n**File:** `test/VisualScenarios.js` — 39 tests across 14 priority scenarios.\n\n| Priority | Scenario | Tests | Status |\n|----------|----------|-------|--------|\n| 1 | IDA* heuristic independence | 2 | ✅ Pass |\n| 2 | No path found (start surrounded) | 4 | ✅ Pass |\n| 3 | Start equals end | 5 | ✅ Pass |\n| 4 | Drag during search (state machine) | 1 | ✅ Documented |\n| 5 | Wall on start/end position | 4 | ✅ Pass |\n| 6 | Pause/Resume cycle | 1 | ✅ Documented |\n| 7 | Restart during search | 1 | ✅ Documented |\n| 8 | JPS all 4 diagonal modes | 4 | ✅ Pass |\n| 9 | Bi-directional vs unidirectional | 1 | ✅ Pass |\n| 10 | Weight parameter effect | 1 | ✅ Pass |\n| 11 | IDA* time limit | 3 | ✅ Pass |\n| 12 | Full grid walls | 3 | ✅ Pass |\n| 13 | Large grid performance (64×36) | 2 | ✅ Pass |\n| 14 | Adjacent start/end | 4 | ✅ Pass |\n\n## Key Findings\n\n1. **Finders don't validate start/end walkability.** They push start into open list unconditionally. Visual app handles this via `isStartOrEndPos` guard in `mousedown` handler.\n\n2. **JPS UI gap confirmed.** Only `IfAtMostOneObstacle` and `Never` exposed. `Always` and `OnlyWhenNoObstacles` work at library level but need UI dropdown to be selectable. Panel.js hardcodes `DiagonalMovement.IfAtMostOneObstacle` at line 139.\n\n3. **State machine correctly guards drag.** `dragStart`/`dragEnd` only allowed from `ready`/`finished` states. No drag possible during `searching`/`paused`.\n\n4. **Pause/resume is clean.** `loop()` checks `Controller.is('searching')` — pausing stops the loop, resume re-enters it from same operations array position.\n\n5. **No \"path not found\" UI feedback.** `view.js:drawPath` returns silently on empty path. `showStats` shows `length: 0` but no explicit message. This is a UI gap, not a library bug.\n\n## Full Suite Result\n\n```\n256 passing (1s)\n0 failing\n```\n\nNo regressions introduced.\n","numLines":51,"startLine":1,"totalLines":51}}}
